,title,link,text,language,family
0,Wik-Me'nh language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wik-Me'nh_language,"Wik-Me'nh is a Paman language of the Cape York Peninsula of Queensland, Australia.",Wik-Keyangan,Australian
1,Music of Australia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Australia,"The music of Australia has an extensive history made of music societies. Indigenous Australian music forms a significant part of the unique heritage of a 40,000- to 60,000-year history which produced the iconic didgeridoo. Contemporary fusions of indigenous and Western styles are exemplified in the works of Yothu Yindi, No Fixed Address, Geoffrey Gurrumul Yunupingu and Christine Anu, and mark ...",Wik-Keyangan,Australian
2,"Wik-Keyangan Language (WIF) - L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map, Endangered ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/wif/,Wik-Keyangan is an extinct language of Australia. It belongs to the Australian language family.,Wik-Keyangan,Australian
3,Wik-Me'nh language explained,https://everything.explained.today/Wik-Keyangan_language/,"Wik-Me'nh is a Paman language of the Cape York Peninsula of Queensland, Australia.",Wik-Keyangan,Australian
4,Kee'ahn - Qld Music Trails,https://qldmusictrails.com/artists/keeahn/,"Kee'ahn is a First Nations musician from North Queensland whose name derives from the Wik word meaning to dance, and to play. Effortlessly blending the sounds of soul, R&B and pop throughout their music, Kee'ahn weaves lush melodies and words reminiscent of heartbreak and healing.",Wik-Keyangan,Australian
5,Wik-Keyangan | Bayala,https://bayala.sl.nsw.gov.au/community/wik-keyangan,Contact Indigenous Team E: info.koori@sl.nsw.gov.au T: +61 2 9273 1577 F: +61 2 9273 1269,Wik-Keyangan,Australian
6,about — KEE'AHN,https://www.keeahn.com/about,"With a name coming from the Wik people, meaning to dance, to play, Kee'ahn honour their name and Ancestors through their soulful music that weaves lush melodies and words reminiscent of heartbreak and healing. Kee'ahn is a proud Yalanji, Jirrbal, Badu islander artist who in 2019 ventured from their home town in North Queensland, to pursue a dream in the Eastern Kulin Nation (Melbourne ...",Wik-Keyangan,Australian
7,Kee'ahn - One Of One - One Of One,https://oneofone.com.au/interviews/keeahn/,"My name derives from the Wik people of Cape York, mob my dad and I have connections to. Kee'ahn derives from a word meaning to dance, to create. This one decision has influenced so much of my life. Growing up in my family meant that I was always singing and dancing and playing music.",Wik-Keyangan,Australian
8,Songs in Australia's First Nations languages - ABC Classic,https://www.abc.net.au/listen/classic/read-and-watch/music-reads/songs-in-australian-first-nations-languages/13963692,"Explore the richness of First Peoples' stories, songs and languages through a selection of classical music featuring languages from different regions across the country.",Wik-Keyangan,Australian
9,AIATSIS AustLang Online,https://aiatsis.gov.au/austlang/language/Y173/name,"If you'd like to share feedback or suggest updates, email us at austlang@aiatsis.gov.au.",Wik-Keyangan,Australian
